    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> for client-style tables (users, providers) with dedicated create/update builders. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Replaces <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>&apos;s generic JSON-based create/update builders with versions that consume the validated (column, value) pairs held by CreateClient_t/UpdateClient_t. Read, delete and search remain inherited from <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>. It also builds the active-flag toggle used to suspend/activate a client and can test whether a username is already taken. Concrete tables (<ref refid="classUser" kindref="compound">User</ref>, <ref refid="classProvider" kindref="compound">Provider</ref>) derive from this class and supply the table name. <simplesect kind="note"><para>All values in generated statements are bound through <ref refid="structBase_1_1Binder" kindref="compound">Binder</ref>; column names come from the validated data_set. The id used by updates/suspends is cached in client_id. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>, <ref refid="structapi_1_1v2_1_1Types_1_1CreateClient__t" kindref="compound">Types::CreateClient_t</ref>, <ref refid="structapi_1_1v2_1_1Types_1_1UpdateClient__t" kindref="compound">Types::UpdateClient_t</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
